R205	Speaker Arg1:T196 Arg2:T195	
R206	Cueing Arg1:T197 Arg2:T195	
R207	Addressee Arg1:T198 Arg2:T195	
T199	Quotation 45494 45615	"One party went by early this morning, and the other, Ivan Ivanitch, put up here for dinner and went on towards evening."
R208	Speaker Arg1:T198 Arg2:T199	
R209	Addressee Arg1:T196 Arg2:T199	
T200	Quotation 45616 45656	"Ah! . . . Has Varlamov been by or not?"
R210	Speaker Arg1:T196 Arg2:T200	
R211	Addressee Arg1:T198 Arg2:T200	
T201	Quotation 45657 45790	"No, Ivan Ivanitch. His clerk, Grigory Yegoritch, went by yesterday morning and said that he had to be to-day at the Molokans' farm."
R212	Addressee Arg1:T196 Arg2:T201	
R213	Speaker Arg1:T198 Arg2:T201	
T202	Quotation 45791 45869	"Good! so we will go after the waggons directly and then on to the Molokans'."
R214	Speaker Arg1:T196 Arg2:T202	
R215	Addressee Arg1:T198 Arg2:T202	
T203	Quotation 45870 45899	"Mercy on us, Ivan Ivanitch!"
T204	Entity 45900 45917	Moisey Moisevitch
T205	Cue 45918 45923	cried
R216	Speaker Arg1:T204 Arg2:T203	
R217	Cueing Arg1:T205 Arg2:T203	
R218	Addressee Arg1:T196 Arg2:T203	
T206	Quotation 45958 46128	"Where are you going for the night? You will have a nice little supper and stay the night, and to-morrow morning, please God, you can go on and overtake anyone you like."
R219	Speaker Arg1:T204 Arg2:T206	
R220	Addressee Arg1:T196 Arg2:T206	
T207	Quotation 46129 46322	"There is no time for that. . . . Excuse me, Moisey Moisevitch, another time; but now I must make haste. We'll stay a quarter of an hour and then go on; we can stay the night at the Molokans'."
R221	Addressee Arg1:T204 Arg2:T207	
R222	Speaker Arg1:T196 Arg2:T207	
