R410	Speaker Arg1:T365 Arg2:T363	
R411	Addressee Arg1:T360 Arg2:T363	
T366	Quotation 62076 62120	"Oh, things in general. What are you doing?"
R412	Addressee Arg1:T365 Arg2:T366	
R413	Speaker Arg1:T360 Arg2:T366	
T367	Quotation 62121 62139	"What am I doing?"
T368	Entity 62140 62147	Solomon
T369	Cue 62148 62156	repeated
R414	Speaker Arg1:T368 Arg2:T367	
R415	Cueing Arg1:T369 Arg2:T367	
R416	Addressee Arg1:T360 Arg2:T367	
T370	Quotation 62189 62411	"The same as everyone else. . . . You see, I am a menial, I am my brother's servant; my brother's the servant of the visitors; the visitors are Varlamov's servants; and if I had ten millions, Varlamov would be my servant."
R417	Speaker Arg1:T368 Arg2:T370	
R418	Addressee Arg1:T360 Arg2:T370	
T371	Quotation 62412 62443	"Why would he be your servant?"
R419	Addressee Arg1:T368 Arg2:T371	
R420	Speaker Arg1:T360 Arg2:T371	
T372	Quotation 62444 62752	"Why, because there isn't a gentleman or millionaire who isn't ready to lick the hand of a scabby Jew for the sake of making a kopeck. Now, I am a scabby Jew and a beggar. Everybody looks at me as though I were a dog, but if I had money Varlamov would play the fool before me just as Moisey does before you."
R421	Speaker Arg1:T368 Arg2:T372	
T373	Entity 62753 62771	Father Christopher
R422	Addressee Arg1:T373 Arg2:T372	
T374	Quotation 62900 62960	"How can you compare yourself with Varlamov, you blockhead?"
T375	Entity 62845 62855	Kuzmitchov
T376	Cue 62893 62898	asked
R423	Cueing Arg1:T376 Arg2:T374	
R424	Speaker Arg1:T375 Arg2:T374	
T377	Entity 62836 62843	Solomon
R425	Addressee Arg1:T377 Arg2:T374	
T378	Quotation 62961 63026	"I am not such a fool as to put myself on a level with Varlamov,"
T379	Cue 63027 63035	answered
T380	Entity 63036 63043	Solomon
R426	Cueing Arg1:T379 Arg2:T378	
R427	Speaker Arg1:T380 Arg2:T378	
R428	Addressee Arg1:T375 Arg2:T378	
T381	Quotation 63083 63399	"Though Varlamov is a Russian, he is at heart a scabby Jew; money and gain are all he lives for, but I threw my money in the stove! I don't want money, or land, or sheep, and there is no need for people to be afraid of me and to take off their hats when I pass. So I am wiser than your Varlamov and more like a man!"
R429	Speaker Arg1:T380 Arg2:T381	
R430	Addressee Arg1:T375 Arg2:T381	
T382	Quotation 63727 63740	"Stop! . . ."
T383	Entity 63741 63759	Father Christopher
