R471	Speaker Arg1:T416 Arg2:T415	
R472	Cueing Arg1:T417 Arg2:T415	
R473	Addressee Arg1:T410 Arg2:T415	
T418	Quotation 65712 65920	"Be so kind as to excuse it, and don't be angry. He is such a queer fellow, such a queer fellow! Oh dear, oh dear! He is my own brother, but I have never had anything but trouble from him. You know he's. . ."
R474	Speaker Arg1:T416 Arg2:T418	
R475	Addressee Arg1:T410 Arg2:T418	
T419	Entity 65921 65938	Moisey Moisevitch
T420	Cue 65978 65985	went on
T421	Quotation 65987 66483	"He is not in his right mind; . . . he's hopeless. And I don't know what I am to do with him! He cares for nobody, he respects nobody, and is afraid of nobody. . . . You know he laughs at everybody, he says silly things, speaks familiarly to anyone. You wouldn't believe it, Varlamov came here one day and Solomon said such things to him that he gave us both a taste of his whip. . . . But why whip me? Was it my fault? God has robbed him of his wits, so it is God's will, and how am I to blame?"
R476	Speaker Arg1:T419 Arg2:T421	
R477	Cueing Arg1:T420 Arg2:T421	
R478	Addressee Arg1:T410 Arg2:T421	
T422	Entity 66507 66524	Moisey Moisevitch
T423	Cue 66535 66544	muttering
T424	Quotation 66574 67073	"He does not sleep at night, and is always thinking and thinking and thinking, and what he is thinking about God only knows. If you go to him at night he is angry and laughs. He doesn't like me either . . . . And there is nothing he wants! When our father died he left us each six thousand roubles. I bought myself an inn, married, and now I have children; and he burnt all his money in the stove. Such a pity, such a pity! Why burn it? If he didn't want it he could give it to me, but why burn it?"
R479	Speaker Arg1:T422 Arg2:T424	
R480	Cueing Arg1:T423 Arg2:T424	
R481	Addressee Arg1:T410 Arg2:T424	
