R624	Addressee Arg1:T553 Arg2:T550	
T554	Quotation 93918 94059	"No, lad, no. It's not from walking. When I walk it seems easier; when I lie down and get warm, . . . it's deadly. Walking is easier for me."
R625	Cueing Arg1:T552 Arg2:T554	
R626	Speaker Arg1:T553 Arg2:T554	
R627	Addressee Arg1:T549 Arg2:T554	
T555	Entity 94219 94221	he
T556	Cue 94240 94251	croaked out
T557	Quotation 94264 94535	"I have no voice. It's a real misfortune. All last night and this morning I have been haunted by the trio 'Lord, have Mercy' that we sang at the wedding at Marionovsky's. It's in my head and in my throat. It seems as though I could sing it, but I can't; I have no voice."
R628	Speaker Arg1:T555 Arg2:T557	
R629	Cueing Arg1:T556 Arg2:T557	
R630	Addressee Arg1:T549 Arg2:T557	
T558	Entity 94536 94538	He
T559	Cue 94575 94582	went on
T560	Quotation 94584 94882	"For fifteen years I was in the choir. In all the Lugansky works there was, maybe, no one with a voice like mine. But, confound it, I bathed two years ago in the Donets, and I can't get a single note true ever since. I took cold in my throat. And without a voice I am like a workman without hands."
