R832	Addressee Arg1:T754 Arg2:T751	
T755	Quotation 121560 121709	"In God's good time we shall set off. There's no starting yet; it is too hot. . . . O Lord, Thy will be done. Holy Mother. . . Lie down, little lad."
R833	Addressee Arg1:T752 Arg2:T755	
R834	Speaker Arg1:T754 Arg2:T755	
T756	Quotation 124387 124428	"All right. . . . Nice gentlefolk, . . ."
T757	Entity 124429 124431	he
T758	Cue 124432 124440	muttered
T759	Quotation 124442 125287	"Took his little lad to school-- but how he is doing now I haven't heard say --in Slavyanoserbsk. I say there is no establishment for teaching them to be very clever. . . . No, that's true -- a nice little lad, no harm in him. . . . He'll grow up and be a help to his father. . . . You, Yegory, are little now, but you'll grow big and will keep your father and mother. . . . So it is ordained of God, 'Honour your father and your mother.' . . . I had children myself, but they were burnt. . . . My wife was burnt and my children, . . . that's true. . . . The hut caught fire on the night of Epiphany. . . . I was not at home, I was driving in Oryol. In Oryol. . . . Marya dashed out into the street, but remembering that the children were asleep in the hut, ran back and was burnt with her children. . . . Next day they found nothing but bones."
