T770	Quotation 128306 128330	"Yes, they were killed,"
T771	Entity 128331 128336	Dymov
T772	Cue 128337 128341	said
T773	Quotation 128355 128833	"Two merchants, father and son, were travelling, selling holy images. They put up in the inn not far from here that is now kept by Ignat Fomin. The old man had a drop too much, and began boasting that he had a lot of money with him. We all know merchants are a boastful set, God preserve us. . . . They can't resist showing off before the likes of us. And at the time some mowers were staying the night at the inn. So they overheard what the merchants said and took note of it."
